{title: Hosanna, Loud Hosanna}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: tune ELLACOMBE}
{columns: 2}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Ho[C]sanna, [G]loud ho[Am]san[G]na
The [F]little [G]children [C]sang[**]
Through [C]pillared [G]court and [Am]tem[G]ple
The [F]lovely [G]anthem [C]rang[**]

To [C]Jesus, [**]who had [G]blessed [**]them
Close [C]folded [**]to his [G]breast[**]
The [C]children [G]sang their [Am]prai[G]ses
The [F]simplest [G]and the [C]best[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
From [C]Oli[G]vet they [Am]fol[G]lowed
'Mid [F]an ex[G]ultant [C]crowd[**]
The [C]victor [G]palm branch [Am]wav[G]ing
And [F]chanting [G]clear and [C]loud[**]

The [C]Lord of [**]earth and [G]hea[**]ven
